{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788638111347742002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"felicific-blueribbon-kitty","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ae02d7b7f168b5e3775853b4dc3d5acd9feb8f8a4464d9e813814c7212fabd26","event_uuid":"1ed60958-38d4-4123-9e01-3ff1ccead009","position":{"commit_sha":"7d8913a9123a28ea578df715c4ddf8ae9a53e3bf","position":"1788637241275139661-1ed60958-38d4-4123-9e01-3ff1ccead009"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"33c1edea4b3291c07adb5d095703eb4ddc99e32babc3d948856ea2927402a830","event_uuid":"f38fbe19-b856-415d-bd99-22c69ec12281","position":{"commit_sha":"aeec8276a862917bbf68bbef66417ceee41877ff","position":"1788637617591993543-f38fbe19-b856-415d-bd99-22c69ec12281"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4d15c06ce1afa8da33f6714952497b5c9b6749814ecd42c831fb643b1b361eab","event_uuid":"51fef1f3-3cbe-451f-93bb-30aab2ed7a82","position":{"commit_sha":"ca072e02beeafc35d95f86f00494616dbfe38c60","position":"1788638111347742001-51fef1f3-3cbe-451f-93bb-30aab2ed7a82"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## How this was found, and the one thing NOT proven\n\nFound while verifying whether Gerrit change 2673 had landed. `git merge-base --is-ancestor 459e1d1b099f origin/main` returned **NO**, but the change HAD merged — as `9e6a0e436520`, found by `Change-Id`. That prompted a sweep of `is-ancestor` uses across the repo, of which this script was the only site where the rewritten sha changes an operator-visible answer.\n\n**Not proven:** I did not establish *why* `feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` was rebased on submit while the other four branches were not. The rebase-on-submit explanation fits (`main` is Rebase-If-Necessary, and the branch is exactly 1 commit ahead of main with its Change-Id present under a different sha), but I did not test the alternative — e.g. the branch tip being an amended patchset never submitted in that exact form, with an equivalent commit landing separately. Whoever claims this should settle that before writing the fix, because it changes whether Change-Id lookup alone is sufficient or whether patch-id equivalence is also needed.\n\n## Store-health context from the same pass\n\n`rebar doctor` on this store: **exit 0**, 0 stale locks, all six lock legs free, all three MCP client configs ok. Its 17 findings are all pre-existing `mis-escalated` link records (blocking-link promotion recording an endpoint that differs from the resolved comparable pair) — unrelated to this bug and not new.\n\nAlso observed and worth a separate look by whoever picks up the \"checks that don't check\" sweep: the CREATE of this ticket returned `push_status: {state: pending, reason: push-transport-failed, detail: \"git timed out after 30s\", unpushed: 3}`, i.e. three ticket commits not yet shared to `origin/tickets`. `rebar doctor` did **not** surface that condition in the output I read. I am flagging this as UNVERIFIED rather than as a finding: I read only the tail of doctor's output, so a sync section may exist above it. If it does not, \"store health command does not report unshared writes\" belongs in the same sweep as this bug — a store that reports healthy while three writes are invisible to every other session is the same failure shape.","timestamp":1788637617591993543},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## How this was found, and the one thing NOT proven\n\nFound while verifying whether Gerrit change 2673 had landed. `git merge-base --is-ancestor\n459e1d1b099f origin/main` returned NO, but the change HAD merged — as `9e6a0e436520`, found by\n`Change-Id`. That prompted a sweep of `is-ancestor` uses across the repo, of which this script\nwas the only site where the rewritten sha changes an operator-visible answer.\n\n**Not proven:** I did not establish WHY `feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` was rebased on submit\nwhile the other four branches were not. The rebase-on-submit explanation fits (`main` is\nRebase-If-Necessary; the branch is exactly 1 commit ahead of main with its Change-Id present\nunder a different sha), but I did not rule out the alternative — an amended patchset never\nsubmitted in that exact form, with an equivalent commit landing separately. Settle that before\nwriting the fix: it decides whether Change-Id lookup alone suffices, or whether patch-id\nequivalence is also needed.\n\n## Store-health context from the same pass\n\n`rebar doctor`: exit 0, 0 stale locks, all six lock legs free, all three MCP client configs ok.\nIts 17 findings are all pre-existing `mis-escalated` link records (blocking-link promotion\nrecording an endpoint that differs from the resolved comparable pair) — unrelated to this bug\nand not new.\n\n## Two observations for the \"checks that don't check\" sweep\n\n1. The CREATE of this ticket returned `push_status: {state: pending, reason:\n   push-transport-failed, detail: \"git timed out after 30s\", unpushed: 3}` — three ticket commits\n   not yet shared to `origin/tickets` — and `rebar doctor` did not surface that condition in the\n   output I read. FLAGGED AS UNVERIFIED, not as a finding: I read only the tail of doctor's\n   output, so a sync section may exist above it. If it does not, \"store reports healthy while\n   writes are invisible to every other session\" is the same failure shape as this bug.\n\n2. The MCP server degraded during this same pass: two `comment_ticket` calls exceeded 120s and\n   were backgrounded, and one then FAILED outright after 300s with \"sent no response or progress\".\n   Tracker writes were completed via the local CLI instead. Recorded here because it is live\n   evidence for `witted-invisible-roan` (MCP endpoint 502s during long gate jobs) and because a\n   silently-dropped MCP write is itself a check-that-does-not-check: the caller's write appears\n   issued and simply never lands.","timestamp":1788638111347742001}],"created_at":1788637241275139661,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"## Summary\n\n`infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh:81` decides whether a feature branch has landed with:\n\n```sh\nif git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$rev\" \"$main_sha\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    state=\"MERGED-BACK\"\nelse\n    state=\"ABANDONED?\"   # not in main's history — either in-flight or truly abandoned\nfi\n```\n\n`main` is **Rebase-If-Necessary**, so Gerrit rebases server-side on submit and the merged commit carries a **different sha** from the branch tip. `is-ancestor` on the pre-rebase tip then returns non-zero and a fully-merged branch is labelled `ABANDONED?`.\n\n## Reproduced on live data (not reasoned)\n\nRun 2026-09-05 against `origin/main = 4c9940348148`, comparing the script's predicate against a Change-Id lookup:\n\n```\nfeature/grounding-t2            MERGED-BACK  tip=709a46e9dbda  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (709a46e9dbda)\nfeature/idea-status             MERGED-BACK  tip=6a28e9a5a6d7  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (6a28e9a5a6d7)\nfeature/llm-provider-seam       MERGED-BACK  tip=5f00bf5253ee  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (5f00bf5253ee)\nfeature/oss-readiness           MERGED-BACK  tip=c4c172914825  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (c4c172914825)\nfeature/s1-windows-sweep-probe  ABANDONED?   tip=9c3c5ba2ea21  ahead=1  change_id_in_main=YES (2e131f2071a0)\n```\n\n**`feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` is the specimen.** Its tip's `Change-Id` is present in `main` as `2e131f2071a0` (\"Make the Windows exclusive-leg tests runnable\") — the work fully landed — yet the inventory reports `ABANDONED?`. The four branches that label correctly simply were not rebased on submit, which is why the defect is intermittent rather than total.\n\n## Severity — deliberately p3, and why\n\nThe error direction is **conservative**. `is-ancestor` under-reports merges; it cannot report an unmerged branch as merged, so nothing here can mark live work safe to delete. Further, `--delete` is gated on **age** (`CAP_DAYS`) plus owner confirmation and does NOT consult `state` at all, so the mislabel does not gate any destructive action.\n\nThe real cost is misdirection: an operator or agent reading `ABANDONED?` for work that already landed may believe the work was lost and attempt to preserve or re-land it — wasted effort, and a duplicate-landing risk. There is a secondary observation worth recording: the computed `state` currently has no effect on the only destructive path, so the check informs a human and nothing else.\n\n## Suggested direction (not prescriptive)\n\nDetermine merged-ness by content/identity rather than by ancestry: look up the tip's `Change-Id` in `main`, or use `git cherry` / `git patch-id` to detect the rebased equivalent. Keep `is-ancestor` as the fast path and fall back when it says no. Distinguish three states rather than two — MERGED-BACK / MERGED-REBASED / NOT-IN-MAIN — so \"rebased and landed\" is not conflated with \"abandoned\".\n\n## Related, and NOT affected\n\nThe ticket close precheck is immune: it scans for a `rebar-ticket:` trailer on a reachable commit (`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`), not for a specific sha, so a rebase-on-submit does not break it. Other `is-ancestor` uses reviewed and found sound in context: `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh:123`, `infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py:129/134` (tracker refs), and the test-suite uses (controlled shas).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A RED test reproduces the mislabel: a branch whose tip is not an ancestor of main but whose Change-Id IS in main is currently reported `ABANDONED?`.\n- [ ] AC2 The detection distinguishes merged-via-rebase from genuinely-not-in-main, and `feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` (or an equivalent fixture) reports as merged.\n- [ ] AC3 No regression in the four branches that already label correctly.\n- [ ] AC4 The relationship between `state` and `--delete` is made explicit — either `state` gates deletion, or the script says plainly that deletion is age-driven and `state` is advisory.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (exit 127) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Terraform may be written and validated but NEVER applied. Do not touch the shared main checkout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3583-a119-db48-412d","ticket_type":"bug","title":"feature-branch-inventory mislabels a rebased-on-submit merged branch as ABANDONED?","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1ed60958-38d4-4123-9e01-3ff1ccead009","f38fbe19-b856-415d-bd99-22c69ec12281","51fef1f3-3cbe-451f-93bb-30aab2ed7a82"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788638111347742002,"uuid":"5f77ca9e-5679-4385-aac2-314d975bc1ba"}